# Muyun — Cursor Rules (暮云思辨投资助手)

Single source of truth: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) (Chinese). Read it before non-trivial work.

## Before any non-trivial work

**Read `skills/muyun-dev-discipline/SKILL.md` first.** Tool-neutral master copy of this project's
engineering discipline gates: fix-in-four-steps, same-class scanning, docs≠fix,
verification-by-running, tuning red lines, pre-commit checklist.
A synced copy also lives in `.cursor/rules/muyun-dev-discipline/`.

Why explicit: skill auto-discovery directories are **not** compatible across agent tools
(`.claude/skills/`, `.github/skills/`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.codex/skills/`, `.workbuddy/skills/`).
This project already lost a mandatory rule that way — the `self-improvement` skill sat only in
`.github/skills/`, so "consult self-improvement after a failure" was never executed.
If you edit the master copy, run `bash scripts/sync-agent-skills.sh`.

## Hard rules

- Lessons must be recorded in `.learnings/LEARNINGS.md` (version controlled). Tool-specific
  session memory does not survive a tool switch or a new machine.
- Docs/comment changes are not fixes. Verify with `git show --stat` that runtime code changed.
- After fixing a bug, scan the whole repo for the same pattern before committing.
- Validate by running, not by reading: full test suite for global-state changes, scripted
  cross-comparison for YAML↔code mappings, known-input→known-output for formulas.
- Virtualenv only: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe`. Never install into a global Python.
